    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: 'Use the BPM input field to change the BPM. Be warned, changing this will
    either skew all current beats, or will outright remove them, so make sure you
    have the right BPM at the start. If the frequency of notes is not high enough,
    increase the BPM by some multiple of its base BPM. So for example, to use quarter
    notes with a BPM of 100, increase the BPM to 400.


    Click on the waveform
    to set the play head position. Press space to play/stop. Click on the editor
    bar to place a note, hold right click to clear any notes under the cursor. Press
    any key whilst the song is playing (other than space or escape) to place a beat
    at the current position in the song. Due to human inaccuracy and input lag, use
    the "Input delay" field to tune where the notes should be placed when you hit
    a key during playtime. For example, an input delay of 0.1 will place the note
    100ms behind the play head. I recommend using the speed slider if you are going
    to place notes while the song is playing, it allows you to accurately place the
    notes without input delay. It also makes the windows for placing notes more lenient'
